+   node held as a local of the (never returning) word; EXIT, R> and RDROP pop one, so EXIT
+   resumes whatever was pushed, exactly like jonesforth.  Past STACK_BYTES, NEXT copies the
+   nodes still on the C stack into `heap` (a stack itself, nodes are never captured), fixes
+   the parents, parks the VM registers and longjmps to main, which restarts on an empty
+   stack.  heap[0] is the bottom node, its own parent, so popping it is harmless.
+   RSP@ copies the newest WINDOW nodes into the cells below R0, newest lowest, so `@` and
+   `8+` can walk them (PRINT-STACK-TRACE, jonesforth's THROW); RSP! pops down to, or pushes
